1. validate_authored_hir.py first run
   RuntimeError: Expected all tensors to be on the same device, but found at
   least two devices, cuda:0 and cpu. The H200-target Module returned evaluator
   values on CUDA while the independently computed oracle remained on CPU.
   The comparison now moves only the oracle to actual.device; no math changed.

2. fft_blind_candidate.py first launch
   ModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'benchmarks'. Running a file under
   scripts/ placed scripts/ rather than the repository root on sys.path. The
   successful command explicitly sets PYTHONPATH=$CONTAINER_WORKSPACE/tileops.

3. TileLang small-N compile warning
   ThreadSync hoisted a sync from an unsafe conditional (tx < 4). The generated
   N=4096 source was inspected and correctness passed; the warning did not alter
   the public output. It is not classified as a TileFoundry gap.
